```text
RESOLUTION NO.  _______

ENTITLED: “A RESOLUTION CERTIFYING PLANNING COMMISSION ACTION
AMENDING THE CHEYENNE AREA FUTURE LAND USE &
TRANSPORTATION MAP OF CONNECT 2045: UPDATE TO THE
MASTER TRANSPORTATION AND FUTURE LAND USE PLAN OF
PLANCHEYENNE, AMENDING THE LAND USE CATEGORY AND
TRANSPORTATION NETWORK FOR
PROPERTY GENERALLY
LOCATED BETWEEN I-25 AND SOUTH GREELEY HIGHWAY, SOUTH
OF COLLEGE DRIVE.”

WHEREAS, PlanCheyenne, as amended by Connect 2045: Update to the Master
Transportation and Future Land Use Plan of PlanCheyenne adopted by the Governing Body of
the City of Cheyenne by Resolution No. 6106, is the Master Plan for the City of Cheyenne and the
Comprehensive Plan for portions of Laramie County adopted by both the Governing Body of the
City of Cheyenne and Laramie County Board of County Commissioners; and

WHEREAS, the intent of the Cheyenne Area Future Land Use & Transportation Map is
not to predetermine specific land uses for individual parcels or specific locations for uses or
facilities, but to provide a general framework for neighborhoods and activity centers organized
around roadway networks and major parks and open space; and

WHEREAS, Brad Emmons of AVI, PC, resident of Cheyenne, has initiated an amendment
to the Cheyenne Area Future Land Use & Transportation Map to amend the land use category
from Urban Residential and Mixed Use Residential to Mixed Use Employment for previously
unplatted land to be known as High Plains Business Park between I-25 and Division Avenue north
of High Plains Road in Cheyenne and Laramie County, Wyoming as shown in Exhibit A which is
attached hereto and incorporated herein; and

WHEREAS, Brad Emmons of AVI, PC, resident of Cheyenne, has initiated an amendment
to the Cheyenne Area Future Land Use & Transportation Map to amend the transportation network
of the land bounded by College Drive on the north, Division Avenue on the east, Terry Ranch
Road on the south, and I-25 on the west as shown in Exhibit B which is attached hereto and
incorporated herein; and

WHEREAS, plan amendments approved by the Governing Body pursuant to the criteria
set forth on Page 18 of PlanCheyenne, as amended; and

WHEREAS, the Laramie County Board of County Commissioners reviewed the proposed
future land use map amendment and were given the opportunity to make comments; and

WHEREAS, a public hearing to receive public input and comments on the proposed
Cheyenne Area Future Land Use & Transportation Map amendment for the above described
property was held before the City of Cheyenne Planning Commission on October 3, 2022 and the
Commission subsequently adopted a resolution approving the proposed amendments; and

By Stefanie Boster at 9:31 am, Oct 05, 2022
