### Page 5 of 14

```text
PLN-22-00010

October 3, 2022
RECOMMENDED MOTION:

Move to adopt the Planning Commission Resolution amending the Cheyenne Area Future Land Use &
Transportation Map amendment for land generally located between I-25 and South Greeley Highway,
south of College Drive.

APPLICABLE CITY CODE SECTION(S) AND PLANS:

•
PlanCheyenne (2014 Community Plan)
•
Connect 2045

BACKGROUND:

The request is to amend the Cheyenne Area Future Land Use & Transportation Map for land generally
located between I-25 and South Greeley Highway, south of College Drive to accommodate the
development of the High Plains Business Park. The area subject to the future land use amendment is roughly
1.5 square miles, but the changes to the transportation network influence nearly 9 square miles of the
southwest section of the community. The land is presently largely undeveloped.

The concurrent applications for an annexation, zoning map amendment, preliminary plat, and final plat have
been submitted. The zoning map amendment will accompany the future land use amendment at Planning
Commission and City Council. If these applications are approved, the applicant will be required to submit a site
plan application for future development.

SURROUNDING LAND USE AND ZONING:

The property subject to the land use map amendment is shown as Mixed-use Residential and Urban
Residential  in the current Cheyenne Area Future Land Use & Transportation Map. These future land use
categories anticipate mostly residential uses with a mix of small-scale, neighborhood-serving
commercial uses.

